Q the dragon crown over Vesh
R a-lore.txt | Vesh is a city of terraced foundries. Its streets climb the mountain in switchbacks lit by amber lamps, and the smiths work through the night because the forges never cool. Pilgrims arrive by the northern road carrying offerings of iron and salt, and the wardens of the gate count every one of them into a ledger bound in dragon's hide. Nobody remembers who first kept the ledger. The ledger is older than the crown, older than the foundries, older than the road itself, and the wardens say the first page is written in a hand no living scribe can read. Some pilgrims come only to see that page. The wardens let them look for the price of one iron nail, and the nails are melted each winter into a new link of the chain that holds the gate. The chain is now so long that it coils twice around the gatehouse, and children of the city count its links on festival days, arguing over the number, because the smiths add links faster than anyone can count them.
R a-lore.txt | The Ember Crown was forged in the caldera of Mount Vesh, where the old dragons slept beneath copper ash. Every king who wore it heard the dragons dreaming.
R f-prompts.md | PROMPT 01 dragon over the foundry city at night, amber lamps
R a-lore.txt | The dragon's pact ended when the last queen broke the crown.
R b-characters.txt | Ilsa Marrow is a cartographer of the foundry city. She carries brass instruments and a map of every switchback in Vesh.\n\nTorvald the Warden keeps the gate ledger. He is old, patient and suspicious of pilgrims with too much salt.
